{
  "$schema": "../../specs/erc7730-v2.schema.json",
  "_curation_note": "PQSigner semantic curation: only the three-argument outbound BORG NTT transfer is admitted for the fixed-block Ethereum NttManager proxy listed by deploymentFormats. It shows every signed operand and native value. recipientChain is the raw Wormhole chain ID and recipient is bytes32, so the display does not invent an EVM address or named destination from mutable peer state. Source fixes refund bytes32 to recipient, disables queuing, and supplies empty transceiver instructions; excess native value is refunded. The six-argument overload remains an exact known-call refusal because arbitrary transceiverInstructions bytes have no injective trusted renderer. Transfer delivery, peers, transceivers, prices, rate limits, queue state, and success remain asynchronous or mutable. Evidence is historical fixed-block source/runtime authority, not destination receipt, live routing, future proxy upgrades, fallback, or blind signing. See tests/erc7730-semantic-evidence/bridge-exits.",
